This session works on two separate repositories located at:

1) Backend (NestJS):
   Path: C:\Nest\eyada
   This is the API and business logic.

2) Frontend (React):
   Path: C:\React\eyada-frontend
   This is the UI that consumes the API.

API Contract:
- The backend Swagger / OpenAPI documentation is available at:
  http://localhost:3000/api
- Swagger is the SINGLE source of truth for all API contracts:
  - Endpoints
  - Request/response schemas
  - DTOs and validation rules

Rules and workflow:
- Always read and rely on the Swagger specification before making changes.
- Any change in backend controllers, DTOs, or Swagger definitions MUST be reflected in the frontend:
  - API service functions
  - TypeScript types/interfaces
  - Forms, UI logic, and error handling
- If a frontend requirement changes:
  - Update backend controllers and DTOs
  - Update Swagger accordingly
  - Then sync the frontend with the updated contract
- Always analyze both repositories before making changes.
- Do not break existing functionality.
- Follow clean code, NestJS best practices, and modern React patterns.

Goal:
Keep backend and frontend fully synchronized at all times using Swagger as the contract reference.
